WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.067
-Chelsea Handler.
Come on.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.567
-Oh, my God.
Hi, you guys!

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.701
-Yeah, oh, my God.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:07.334
They love you.
-Hi, guys!

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:09.634
Look at this handsome array
of men.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:10.901
-Yeah, we do have a good crew
over there.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:14.267
-There's a party over there.
-Yeah, it is. It is.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.501
I want to get into "Revolution,"

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.634
your stand-up special
on Netflix.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:19.667
It's fantastic.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.334
But first,
we have things to cover.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.868
You're hosting
the Critics Choice Awards.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.100
-I am. Sunday night.
We gotta keep the vibes fun.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's fun.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.067
-I'm excited.
Yeah.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.234
I mean, people are safer now
around me,

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.467
since I've been to therapy.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.367
They don't have to fear,
you know?

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.133
I'm not gonna go in there
and skewer people.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.734
I think it needs to be
a really fun night.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.267
You do it really well.
-Yeah. Oh, thank you.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.634
-And I'm gonna just copy
what you do.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.834
-Oh, that's perfect.
That's Sunday night then.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.868
-Yeah, Sunday night.
Critics Choice Awards.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:47.167
I'm really excited.
That's gonna be fun.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:50.667
-But then, also, if you love
Chelsea Handler like I do,

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:51.834
you get to see more of you.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.567
You're also guest hosting
on "The Daily Show."

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.767
-Oh, yes.
I'm excited about that, too.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-People are talking about that

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.534
'cause, they're like,
that's gonna be great.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.801
-Yeah, I have a lot of people
that I need to go off on

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:05.234
in, like, a public forum,
so I'm gonna save it.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.200
and skip this
Critics Choice Awards for that

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.334
because these
are Hollywood people.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.767
You know how sensitive
everyone is.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.767
And then I'm just gonna go
straight for the jugular

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.634
when I get over
to "The Daily Show."

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:17.167
-When you do your special --
"Revolution," by the way --

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.467
when you do that,
you talk about your family.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:21.100
You're very specific.
You talk about

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.767
a lot of people in your family.
-Yes.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.467
-Do they get upset?
And they go,

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.000
"Hey, wish you didn't
bring that up"?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.968
-No, I give them a warning now.
As I've learned over the years,

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:32.067
it's more sensitive of me
to tell them that it's happening

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.434
before it happens,
but still do it.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.501
[ Laughter ]
And like I said to my nephew,

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.834
I said this time
I have a whole run about him.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.200
-It's so funny.
-And I told him when he

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.267
came to see me perform, I said,
"Listen, Jakey --"

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.200
he's my firstborn nephew, so,
you know, he's sensitive, too.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.634
And I said,
"There's a bit about you,

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:51.267
and it's not pleasa--
you know, it's not flattering."

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:54.367
And he said, "Okay."
And then he saw the show.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.467
And then afterwards, I said, "So
how did you feel about that?"

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.734
'Cause if it's a real issue,
maybe we can discuss

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.267
pretending to take it out.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:03.267
And he was like, "No,
everything you said was true."

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.934
And I was like, "All right.
Way to man up. Great."

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:08.167
-Wow, he grew up a little bit.
-Yeah.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:11.400
-But you also --
you talk about family.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.667
You poke fun at yourself a lot
in this special.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.367
I told you some jokes
that I love backstage.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:20.501
But can you explain the one
where you went to Africa?

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.400
-Well, okay.
The reason why --

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.534
I'm very outspoken about
not wanting to be a parent

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.267
because I don't think
I have the skills that --

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:29.133
you know, I'm not equipped with
what it takes to answer

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.801
all of those questions
to children,

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.234
because they don't
just ask you once.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.000
They come in and in and in.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.100
I have enough nieces and nephews
to know that I don't have

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.634
the tolerance for that kind of
line of questioning

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:42.300
about things that I really don't
even know the answers to.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.067
And at a certain age, when you
don't know answers to questions,

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.734
it's too embarrassing to ask
questions, you know?

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.400
You just have to pretend
you know.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.534
And I talk about a story that I
didn't know -- and this is true.

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.200
I didn't know until
I was 40 years old

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.267
that the sun and the moon
were not the same thing.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:02.767
-I found this hard to believe.

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.601
What are you talking about?

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.133
-It was shocking to me, as well.
I mean --

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.400
[ Laughter ]
-Of course.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.701
It must have been more shocking
to you.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.400
-I was like -- I was in Africa.
We were on safari.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.367
My sister and I
were riding an elephant,

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.901
and there was a man
riding an elephant for us

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.000
because we don't know
how to ride an elephant.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.300
And my older sister, Simone,
looked up at the sky,

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.367
and she said, "Chelsea,
Chelsea, look up.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.901
It's not often
you get to see the sun

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:30.434
and the moon at the same time."
-Yeah.

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.968
-And I was like --
I was like Scooby-Doo.

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:38.868
I'm like, "Ruh, wah?"
I said, I go, "Wait.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.934
But they're always together."
And as soon as I said that,

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:42.200
she turned around, and she goes,
"What did you say?"

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.067
And I was like, "Oh, shut up,
shut up, shut up."

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:45.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:48.901
I knew what I said I was wrong.
-Giddyup, elephant.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:51.067
-I was like, "Let's canter.
Is that what an elephant does?"

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.901
-Oh, my God.
-And she looked at me,

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:54.968
she goes, "I need you --"

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.367
And I just tried
to gloss over it.

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:58.234
I was like,
"Never mind what I said.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:01.534
I know." And she said,
"No. I need you to tell me

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:05.267
what you think is happening
between the sun and the moon."

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:07.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.868
And I was like,
"Honestly, I just assumed

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:13.033
when the sun went down,
it popped back up as the moon,"

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:14.200
you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.701
-Did a little costume change.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.100
-I'm like,
"Is that not what's happening?"

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.534
The man riding the elephant
spoke no English and went,

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.801
"Pfft!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.934
And he's just like, "Another
dumb American," you know?

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:29.267
-You also talk about your dogs.
-Yeah, you have a dog, Gary.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:30.534
I talk about my dog, Gary.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:31.701
But I didn't know
you had a dog, Gary.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:34.434
-How big is your dog, Gary?
-Well, Gary --

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.701
I know also a reason
I shouldn't have children

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:39.501
is because I've rescued
nine dogs in my life.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:40.834
Thank you.
That's sweet.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:45.300
Thank you, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.834
And I've returned four.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:48.334
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.400
My goodness.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.267
-And Gary
was a return to sender.

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:52.934
So, I got
a Bernese mountain dog.

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:54.567
I went to a dog show in London,

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.033
and I saw
a Bernese mountain dog.

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:58.000
And I have a type.
I like dogs --

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.000
I don't want to be -- I don't
like overactive dogs.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.601
I like them to be
overweight and lazy.

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.434
-Okay.
That's your type of dog.

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:08.734
-I don't want to go for hikes
or walks or any of that, really.

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:11.000
I just want to get home,
you know, snuggle at the end

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.934
of a long day, and then
when it gets too hot be like,

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.601
"Get the hell off of me."
That's what I'm looking for.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:18.467
So, yeah, I got a dog --
I saw a Bernese mountain dog.

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:20.267
And, you know, as you know,
when you're a celebrity,

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:21.601
you can't buy dogs.

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.601
You have to rescue
all of your animals.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:24.767
You have to.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.000
Otherwise, PETA will
burn your house down.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.634
So I said to my assistant,
"You need to find me

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:34.767
a used Bernese mountain dog."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.400
And he -- it was impossible.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.834
So, I ended up buying this dog,
and he came into my life.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:41.167
And he was a puppy,
and he was exactly the opposite

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:42.667
of everything I was looking for.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.367
He ate everything.
He jumped on everything.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:47.968
My other two dogs moved upstairs
as soon as he came home.

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.400
They didn't come down
for two days.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.200
They were like,
"Let us know when Gary's gone."

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:53.467
-They didn't want
any part of it.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:56.033
-Yeah. So, I had to give Gary
to another person

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.067
because I couldn't handle
the situation.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:05:59.501
And, yeah.
So, I'm not --

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:02.167
And I know that you can't
do that with babies, you know?

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.868
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:05.367
-Especially if you're
a public person.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:08.000
You will definitely get caught.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.100
-But there's
a happy ending for Gary.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.767
-Gary lives with a woman
named Teresa.

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:14.267
She sends -- I pay for his
clothing and education and --

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:17.834
-His clothing.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:17.834 --> 00:06:19.467
He's a really smart dresser.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:21.901
What's up with your dog, Gary?
What kind of dog is it?

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:25.868
-It's a golden retriever, and
she's just the best, nicest dog.

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:28.367
My dog doesn't bark.
-But why is her name Gary?

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:32.033
-She was on the show --
She was an actor puppy.

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:33.767
-Okay.
-And her name was Gary.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.834
We didn't have time
to get a female or male dog.

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:36.901
-Okay. Well, great.

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:38.267
Well, everything's fluid now
anyway.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:39.934
She's right on time.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:42.968
-She's a very topical dog.
That's true, it is very --

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:46.767
It makes sense.
Before we show --

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:48.868
Before we show a clip
from your special,

00:06:48.868 --> 00:06:50.033
would you like to set this up?

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:51.701
-Oh, yes.
This is a perfect example.

00:06:51.701 --> 00:06:53.767
So, my brother
was seeing my show.

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:56.167
You run the show several --
a hundred times

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.033
before you film it
for your special, usually.

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:00.634
So, my brother kept coming
to shows, my older brother,

00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:02.534
one of my older brothers,
and he said, he goes,

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:05.200
"You're talking about Simone,
our sister, a lot in your act."

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.968
And I said, "Are you jealous?"
He goes, "Well, I mean,

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:09.000
you should share the love."
I'm like, "Oh, you want me to

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.434
write a joke about you?
'Cause I can."

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:11.534
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.367
-And then this is --
this is that joke.

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:14.634
-Okay, here we go.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.400
-I was with my brother
the other day, and I said,

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.133
"Why are you even a parent?"

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:21.067
I said,
"You're not very good at it."

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:23.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:27.434
He said, "Chelsea, I had
to think about my legacy."

00:07:27.434 --> 00:07:29.801
I said, "Who are you talking to?
Is someone behind me?

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.167
What are you talking --"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:33.701
"You want to think about your --
who the [bleep] are you

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:35.100
to think about your legacy?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.133
Who do you think you are..."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:40.133
"...that people are waiting
to see what you leave behind

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:41.968
on this Earth?

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:44.267
Your legacy is that
you're my [bleep] brother."

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:46.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:48.501
-Oh, come on!

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.534
"You want to be in the act?

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:52.033
You want to be in the act,
buddy?

00:07:52.033 --> 00:07:53.200
I'll put you in the act."

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.834
Chelsea handler, everybody!

00:07:54.834 --> 00:07:58.434
"Revolution" is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:07:58.434 --> 00:08:01.133
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

